                                                                                
 Usage: codemonkey [OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...                                  
                                                                                
 codemonkey — a scriptable coding-agent CLI for OpenAI-style and                
 Anthropic-style endpoints (defaults to a local llama.cpp server).              
                                                                                
╭─ Options ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ --version                                      Print the version and exit.   │
│ --provider                      -p      <str>  Provider for the interactive  │
│                                                session.                      │
│ --model                         -m      <str>  Model override for the        │
│                                                interactive session.          │
│ --sandbox                               <str>  Sandbox level for the session │
│                                                (read-only | workspace-write  │
│                                                | danger-full-access).        │
│ --ask-for-approval,--approval   -a      <str>  Approval policy (untrusted |  │
│                                                on-request | never).          │
│ --add-dir                       -C      <str>  Additional writable directory │
│                                                (repeatable).                 │
│ --max-turns                             <int>  Max agent turns per prompt.   │
│                                                [default: 0]                  │
│ --timeout                               <int>  Per-tool timeout seconds.     │
│                                                [default: 0]                  │
│ --ignore-user-config                           Skip                          │
│                                                ~/.codemonkey/config.yaml.    │
│ --dangerously-bypass-approval…                 Lift the sandbox and approval │
│                                                gates entirely.               │
│ --show-reasoning                               Print model reasoning blocks  │
│                                                in the REPL.                  │
│ --ephemeral                                    Do not persist this session.  │
│ --help                                         Show this message and exit.   │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
╭─ Commands ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ config         Print the effective merged config (secrets masked).           │
│ review         LLM review of the repo's uncommitted diff (read-only).        │
│ graph          Print code-graph facts for SYMBOL from graphify-out/ (no      │
│                model needed).                                                │
│ undo           Undo: restore the most recent checkpoint (files snapshotted   │
│                pre-mutation).                                                │
│ rollback       Rollback a change plan whole (loop41): restore pre-plan       │
│                bytes, delete                                                 │
│                plan-created files. `undo` keeps file semantics; this is the  │
│                plan verb.                                                    │
│ eval           Run a golden evaluation suite against the real exec path.     │
│ digest         Plain-text digest of one run (thread).                        │
│ rules-compile  Journal failures → draft permission rules.                    │
│ status         Operator surface: aggregate                                   │
│                jobs/journal/sessions/eval/cost/spill.                        │
│ models         List models exposed by a provider endpoint.                   │
│ sessions       List persisted sessions (thread id, updated time, first       │
│                prompt).                                                      │
│ evidence       Evidence pack (loop45, cycle 105): a run's claims bound to    │
│                the journal                                                   │
│                records behind them, hash-chained so edits fail verification. │
│ branch         Worktree branches in .branches/.                              │
│ journal        Execution-journal forensics.                                  │
│ jobs           Durable, resumable job files.                                 │
│ lessons        Lessons learned from run history.                             │
│ redact         Secret-redaction repair pass.                                 │
│ budget         VRAM→tokens budget calculator.                                │
│ skills         Quarantined skill store.                                      │
│ exec           Non-interactive exec: run the agent once, print the final     │
│                response. Use `exec resume [--last|THREAD_ID] [PROMPT]` to    │
│                continue a session.                                           │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

